  "body_html": "<h1>Prisoner's Dilemma</h1>\n<p>The Prisoner's Dilemma is a two-player strategic game where each player can\nCooperate ($C$) or Defect ($D$). The payoff matrix is:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>$C$</th>\n<th>$D$</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>$C$</td>\n<td>(2, 2)</td>\n<td>(0, 3)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>$D$</td>\n<td>(3, 0)</td>\n<td>(1, 1)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Defecting is a weakly dominant strategy for each player. The unique Nash\nequilibrium is $(D, D)$ with payoff $(1, 1)$, which is Pareto-dominated by\n$(C, C)$ with payoff $(2, 2)$.</p>",
